Package: doobr
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Simulation of Future Sample Paths for Scenario Generation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tommaso", "Ferrario", role = "aut"),
    person("Alan", "King", role = "aut"),
    person("Enza", "Messina", role = "aut"),
    person("Matteo", "Pelagatti", , "matteo.pelagatti@unimib.it", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Hongyu", "Zhang", role = "aut"))
Description: Generates future sample paths and scenario trees for a univariate
    time series without assuming a parametric data generating process. Any
    learner may supply the conditional mean and conditional scale; the
    innovations are resampled from an honest bank of out-of-fold standardised
    residuals obtained by purged K-fold cross-fitting, so that the simulated
    increments form a martingale difference sequence rather than inheriting the
    optimism of in-sample residuals. Provides martingale-difference tests for
    both estimation steps and calibration tests for the simulated paths.
